WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:02.461
Detective Danner:
Hit me with that Aniq sequel.

00:00:02.461 --> 00:00:03.587
This is not a sequel.

00:00:03.587 --> 00:00:05.005
Sounds like a sequel to me.

00:00:05.923 --> 00:00:09.718
What was true in season one and
was again true this season is
that…

00:00:10.177 --> 00:00:11.345
Ahhh!

00:00:11.345 --> 00:00:12.888
There’s another murder.

00:00:12.888 --> 00:00:13.722
(Gasp)

00:00:13.722 --> 00:00:15.224
♪♪

00:00:15.224 --> 00:00:16.266
We love murder.

00:00:16.266 --> 00:00:18.518
-We’re drawn to it, one might
say.
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.187
What?!

00:00:20.187 --> 00:00:22.940
We get a bunch of new suspects
and characters.

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:25.359
Look at all the people losing
their heads.

00:00:25.817 --> 00:00:26.443
(Groans)

00:00:26.443 --> 00:00:27.236
(Laughing)

00:00:27.236 --> 00:00:29.071
All the casting is so on point.

00:00:29.363 --> 00:00:32.157
Christopher Miller:
The person who was the killer, I
told them that they were the killer.

00:00:32.157 --> 00:00:34.201
Everybody else I didn’t say one
way or the other.

00:00:34.201 --> 00:00:35.494
Anna Konkle:
Every actor thought it was
themselves.

00:00:35.494 --> 00:00:36.453
Elizabeth Perkins: 
Because we’re so self-involved.

00:00:36.453 --> 00:00:37.579
Yeah, we’re so self-involved. 

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:38.455
Like, oh, please be me.

00:00:38.455 --> 00:00:39.957
Ooh, I probably did it.

00:00:39.957 --> 00:00:40.457
I did it!

00:00:40.457 --> 00:00:41.750
I also killed Edgar!

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:44.086
I strangled him with my bare
hands!

00:00:44.086 --> 00:00:44.795
He was poisoned.

00:00:44.795 --> 00:00:47.381
I poisoned Edgar with my bare
hands!

00:00:48.131 --> 00:00:51.176
By episode eight I was like I
know who did this.

00:00:51.176 --> 00:00:53.762
I do know a suspect when I see
one.

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:57.140
Then when I got to find out who
did it, I was wrong.

00:00:57.975 --> 00:01:02.020
This season, we decided to
really push the genres even
farther.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:04.690
You’re waist deep in the same
dirty deal as your womb fruit.

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:07.651
Zach Woods:
It’s a fun challenge of the show
that you’re not just playing

00:01:07.651 --> 00:01:11.571
a genre but you’re playing the
subjectivity of the person
whose episode it is.

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.824
You are madder than a mad hatter
at a hat haberdashery.

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:15.701
What-ho revelers!

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:18.745
It was maybe one of the most
magical acting moments of my
life.

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:19.913
Yes, John Cho.

00:01:20.414 --> 00:01:22.666
I think people are going to fall
in love with these characters

00:01:22.666 --> 00:01:25.669
while also getting to play that
game of whodunnit with
each other.

00:01:25.794 --> 00:01:26.461
So... 

00:01:28.213 --> 00:01:29.840
Christopher Miller:
And cut! 
I think we got it.

00:01:30.674 --> 00:01:32.134
They’re always surprising you,
Lord and Miller.

00:01:32.342 --> 00:01:33.844
And the stakes couldn’t be
higher.

00:01:34.136 --> 00:01:34.970
(Cheering)

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:37.431
♪"It's my party" 
By Lesley Gore♪

00:01:38.515 --> 00:01:41.560
It’s everything you loved about
the first season and a bunch of
new stuff.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:44.062
♪♪

00:01:44.062 --> 00:01:44.646
Yeah!

00:01:44.646 --> 00:01:45.397
Go! Go! Go!

00:01:45.397 --> 00:01:48.066
♪♪

00:01:48.066 --> 00:01:49.776
This is juicy!

00:01:50.277 --> 00:01:54.156
♪You would cry too if it happened
to you. ♪

00:01:54.156 --> 00:01:54.823
-Ahh!
-Ha ha!

